<title>CHINA: China, Airbus ink $300 mln deal for 10 A320S.</title>
<headline>China, Airbus ink $300 mln deal for 10 A320S.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>China Northwest Airlines and China Aviation Supplies Corp on Friday signed a $300 million agreement to buy 10 A320s from Airbus Industrie, the Xinhua news agency said.  </p>
<p>The three parties signed the agreement in Beijing, Xinhua said.</p>
<p>Deliveries are due to begin in the year 2000, it said.</p>
<p>Each A320 will have 150 economy-class seats and eight first-class seats, the agency said.</p>
<p>It gave no further details.</p>
</text>
